{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1474339-\u00e6on-rule-questions-about-thermokinesis","id":1474339,"title":"[\u00c6on] Rule questions about Thermokinesis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-09T17:19:00-08:00","id":1474339,"title":"[\u00c6on] Rule questions about Thermokinesis","content":"Hello<br /> <br /> I have two rules question about the Thermokinesis power Flash and Sheath.<br /> My players character got Thermokinesis at 3 dots.<br /> <br /> So according to the second level power <b>Flash </b>and their higher mode knowledge this get's an additional Enhancement to the mode dot level enhancement the power gives them as lowel level modes receive additional enhancments by the difference in their mode knowledge? i.e a Thermokinetic that knows the mode at 2 and uses Flash will have +2 Enhancements, meanwhile when the Thermokinetic know the mode at 3 thew will have +4 Enhancents. <br /> Is that correct?<br /> <br /> <b>Sheath</b><br /> Sheath - especially the ice variant gives powerful armor on par with a spiderharness and/or VARG system and with enough success outshines them - does the power stack with any worn armor? I'd say yes. at least with the hard armor. or does one only get the highest armor rating from any kind of armor?<br /> <br /> Honestly I do not really understand how the fire variant should provide hard armor - but i rather see it automatically have the defensive tag...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T18:52:35-08:00","id":1474344,"title":"","content":"I think your Enhancement is too high unless the character is getting Enhancement from another source. They should gain Enhancement equal to the difference between the Mode Dot they're using and their Mode Dots known. So if they know Sheath (3 Dots) and use Flash (2 Dots), they gain 1 Enhancement to Flash (3-2=1). If they used Equilibrium (1 Dot), they'd get 2 Enhancement, while using Distant Touch (0 Dots) would grant 3 Enhancement.<br /> <br /> Other ways to gain Enhancement would be the Favored Mode Edge (+2 Enhancement for a single Mode), a Psionic Connection to the target (+1 Enhancement), or combining Psionic Aptitudes with a Vitakinetic (Enhancement equal to the Vitakinetic's Psi when using your power on a living creature).<br /> <br /> I believe you don't usually combine different sources of armor unless the entry specifically lets you, like with the Tough Cookie Edge. Otherwise everyone would just wear multiple types of armor layered onto each other. If you REALLY want a lot of armor, stop by the Aesculapian Order's HQ and get Dr. Zweidler to give you 12+ points of Scale 2 soft armor; it'll last a week. This is probably how the orders did so well against the Australian Aberrant attack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T20:51:53-08:00","id":1474350,"title":"","content":"The thing about Flash and a few other powers is that they all use the same roll to attack and activate the power, while other attacks, like BK growing weapons from their hands, use a roll to activate the power (create a weapon) and one to attack. Also, the roll to activate AND attack uses a dice pool that was not optimised at char gen (you will not roll 10 dice here for quite a while after char gen). Also, only the highest power of VK can increase your dice pool in that roll, while 3 dots can do the same in BK option.<br /> <br /> The result is, at start, the roll will spend 1+ successes to activate the power and then spend successes to beat defense, so you will have less successes than first expected. In higher levels it is amazingly lethal and precise and the enhancements are great to beat scale gap to a Nemesis Aberrant, or a small ship.<br /> <br /> For Sheath it should stack over any armor, including the ones granted by Perikinesis. To be honest, it is fighting against many other defensive powers to say which one is the best defensive power, as many are great (alertness, from Clair, is the best as it is free, permanent and grants defense and not armor, in my opinion).<br /> <br /> A Legionary is supposed to be a walking war machine, capable of fighting anything, from a Nova in space to a ship or even a small fleet. It is not supposed to be used against other people, at least not regular people, it is supposed to be used to open holes in a ship hull and resist a cannon shot. A Nova can do better, but still\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T14:37:58-08:00","id":1474923,"title":"","content":"Okay - NPC da do not have any kind Soft armor / defense. Will be easily made a crisp when facing a psychokinetic with thermokinesis 3+ - which is easily on par with having a rifle/carabiner. <br /> <br /> Yeah the Legionaire in my game - is now through the second fight completly unharmed thanks to Sheath. Meanwhile the clear &amp; the ditto got roughed up a lot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T16:22:18-08:00","id":1474925,"title":"","content":"A good houserule is to assume half of an antagonist's defense comes from soft armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}